15. Evaluate Transactional Outbox

If Kafka publication must not be lost after a successful database transaction, evaluate:

Business Transaction
        │
        ├── Business tables
        │
        └── Outbox table
               │
               ▼
           DB COMMIT
               │
               ▼
        Outbox Publisher
               │
               ▼
             Kafka

This prevents:

DB COMMIT succeeds
       ↓
Application crashes
       ↓
Kafka event never published

The outbox publisher should use:

* Batch reads
* Row claiming
* Multiple workers
* Efficient indexes
* Retry
* Idempotent publishing
* Status tracking

Do not introduce an outbox automatically if Kafka itself is already the authoritative durable event source. Determine the existing business semantics first.

